Translation patch: libsignal_protocol::session_core (new module)

Change: the new module `session_core` (declared in `lib.rs`) holds nine functions and one private logging function. Each function is a stretch of `process_prekey` or `process_prekey_bundle` between two store calls, moved out of `session.rs`: the trust check, the two signature checks, the initiator's key choice and session set-up, the responder's session lookup, version check, Kyber prekey ID check, Kyber ciphertext check and session set-up. The `log::info!` of `process_prekey_bundle` moves into the private function `log_unacknowledged_pre_key_message`. The two call-site patches `protocol-session-process_prekey` and `protocol-session-process_prekey_bundle` call the functions.
Why: both callers are `async` and call the application's stores, so Charon cannot translate them, and the extraction leaves out the `session` module (protocol-lib-store_api.patch). The code between the store calls has no `async` and no store. In its own module the extraction can translate it. Aeneas stops on `log!` expansions, so the logging function is opaque in the extraction, as the logging functions of `double_ratchet.rs` are.
Behaviour: the same code runs in the same order, and the callers keep every store call in its original place (see the two call-site patches). The moved code has the same effects, with three differences of form. `choose_initiator_keys` clones the Kyber prekey of the bundle before the caller asks the store for its identity key pair, where the original cloned it after that call, when it built the parameters. `required_kyber_ciphertext` returns the reference that the original kept in a local variable. The log record of the initiator carries the module path `libsignal_protocol::session_core` and the line of the new function, where the original record carried `libsignal_protocol::session`.
Relies on: protocol-pqxdh-RecipientParameters.patch

